    "warnings": [
      "Positive definiteness of `B.toQuadraticMap` controls only `B(x,x)` and does not require `B` to be symmetric. For a nonsymmetric `B`, the derivative of `B(r,r)` contains both `B(A_u(v),r)` and `B(r,A_u(v))`, so the stated one-sided `IsFOCP` and `hessianTerm` are not generally the gradient and Hessian conditions of the advertised objective. The selected theorem correctly covers ordinary inner products as a special case, but the claimed extension to every positive-definite bilinear form is not justified as an optimization statement. Add a symmetry hypothesis to Lean, or revise the prose to describe the nonsymmetric case as an algebraic extension whose predicates need not be objective criticality."
    ]
  },
